reading:
Pocket Timeline has been judged once: main round 11, last of 17 at 5.11 (today's page scored 4.71). It was in no judge's top four and got no promise votes. Nothing sank the idea itself. All eight lenses said to keep the NOW / NEXT / LATER spine. Feedback called it "line art the owner would enjoy", system "a strong structural rule that could run through every page", and interaction "a strong way to tell time at a glance". Usability also praised Plans' week agenda with "Nothing on.". Style scored it 6.3 and called it "the most personality in the room".

What sank it was the Game Boy costume:
- **Pixel faces on everything people read.** Page titles, section heads and item names were in pixel faces. Type gave 4.2: Pixelify item names wrap ("Oaks Park / roller rink"), and Silkscreen's wide tracked caps make "IN 10 DAYS" loud. Usability found "Oaks Park" reading as "Ooks Pork" and "29" as "89".
- **A four-green ground.** The moss and olive ground (17,26,17), with khaki card fills, made the page more monochrome, not less (soul 5, skeptic 4.3, system 5).
- **Chunky frames.** Double khaki frames with hard 4px shadows are the heavy plain boxes the owner dislikes.
- **Berry pink.** It marked NOW and "was due", where it reads as an alarm.
- **Usability faults.** There were 7 small targets on Home and 25 on To do, and late was not shown on the To do page. The pixel icons could not be recognised, the month grid shrank into a small tube, and the right side of the bar had icons with no words.

The soul lens named the deeper loss: the light was a handheld LCD's, not a tube's.

The owner's own notes point the way. They love fine line art that carries time and order through every page. They want glow that is lit data where the phosphor is, with the rest grounded. So the lineage wins if:
- the spine becomes a fine, lit line through every page;
- the costume is cut back to a friendly handheld accent (the lens-shaped tube, her name plate on the box, the cartridges, square stops, the dotted future);
- the ground goes back to green-black, with slate for solids;
- only live things glow: the NOW and NEXT lamps, the tubes, the key word and Send;
- the tube draws the family's time;
- late shows as amber words on To do, the chat has two sides, no target is under 44px, and the title names the planner's job.

This heat has two other line lineages, Track and Night Timetable. Pocket must keep what is its own: one vertical spine of time with square NOW / NEXT / LATER stops and a dotted tail for later.
